  "question": {
    "text": "A ray of light passing through the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;reflects on the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>-axis at point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and the reflected ray passes through the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;be the point that divides the line segment <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;internally into the ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. Let the co-ordinates of the foot of the perpendicular&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math> from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;on the bisector of the angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. Then, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#946;</mi></math>&nbsp;is equal to _____.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "31",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/9887b846-8ed2-49a0-8be7-04dd6d27f577-image.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 192px;\" /></p><p>By observation we know the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></math>-coordinate of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8943;</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Now&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;is image of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;which will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>&nbsp; Equation of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;</p><p>i.e.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>14</mn></math></p><p>Now&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;meets&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo></math>axis at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math></p><p>so&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>23</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;by solving with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>23</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8943;</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>By&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math>, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>23</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>31</mn></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
